// A program that *requires* input content: `int` over an empty buffer has
// nothing to parse, so it faults — and the fault must say where and what it
// wanted (§7.11). `reads_lines_of_int.px` is the other half of the pair, where
// empty input has an answer (`[]`) rather than a mismatch.
fn main() {
    let n = read int
    out(n)
}
